[Music]  the title is a result of the  geopolitical dimension of resilience  taking center stage in our second annual  foresight report with this report we ask  ourselves what it means to take the eu's  open strategic autonomy and the global  leadership to the next level in an  increasingly multiple global order  we looked at four structural mega trends  that will have a significant impact on  the eu on its path towards 2050 namely  climate change and other environmental  challenges  digital hyper connectivity and  technological transformations  pressure on democracy and values  and shifts in the global order and  demography  we have identified 10 areas where eu  action could enhance our open strategic  autonomy and global leadership giving us  the best possible chance of achieving  our long-term policy objectives like  reaching climate neutrality by 2050  [Music]  all eu actions across the 10 identified  areas are interconnected  for example to ensure the health of eu  citizens we are building a european  health union that invests in health  workers innovative care models and new  technologies  to ensure this is sustainable we need to  secure sufficient supplies of  decarbonized and affordable energy but  also over critical components without  creating new dependencies on raw  materials  [Music]  strategic foresight involves exploring  scenarios identifying trends and  emerging issues using them to steer  better informed decisions and acting in  the present to shape the future  foresight is not a crystal ball however  and we cannot know exactly what that  future might hold  but with a better understanding of the  mega trends at play and the related  uncertainties and opportunities we can  make more ambitious strategic choices  today in pursuit of our global  leadership as we head towards 2050.  the strategic foresight reports will  also inform the annual state of the  union addresses and the commission work  programs  [Music]

